  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Let $f(n)$ be maximal such that there exists a set $A$ of $n$ points in $\\mathbb{R}^2$ in which every $x\\in A$ has at least $f(n)$ points in $A$ equidistant from $x$.\nIs it true that $f(n)\\leq n^{o(1)}$? Or even $f(n) < n^{O(1/\\log\\log n)}$?",
